7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]\"targeting\" state, <enter> offers a single-keypress \"save to the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]targeted xprompt\" option, and saving writes the correct file [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](chezmoi source included) and then offers exactly the follow-up [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]actions that file needs — commit/push, a scoped chezmoi apply, or [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the matching `sase memory init` / `sase skill init`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]xprompt_target_mode.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/xprompt_target_mode.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-hp[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-hp/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Targeting model, reference identity, and chezmoi-aware write [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]paths[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]target[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]target: harden XPromptBinding into a full targeting record (canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reference form, resolved chezmoi write path, apply target, cheap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stat-only staleness), add the single target/clear choke point on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PromptInputBar, and route bound writes through the resolved write path.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Every definition-load surface targets its xprompt[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after target[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]surfaces: audit every path that loads an xprompt definition into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt stack, add the missing \"edit definition here\" action to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Select XPrompt panel, stop the external-editor round trip from silently [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dropping the target, and lock the audit down with an invariant test.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Target-aware <enter> chooser with a single-key save[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]menu[dim] · [dim][/dim]after target[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]menu: open the submit chooser whenever the stack is multi-pane or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]targeted, and add the single-key \"save to the targeted xprompt\" and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"save as a new xprompt\" rows with dirty/clean-aware copy.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Post-write follow-up actions with memory and skill init [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]integration[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]followup[dim] · [dim][/dim]after target[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]followup: replace the single commit/push confirmation with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classifier-driven follow-up chooser that offers commit/push, a scoped [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chezmoi apply, `sase memory init`, or `sase skill init` — whichever [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]actually apply to the written file — and runs them through the tracked [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task queue.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Visual language for the targeting state[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]visual[dim] · [dim][/dim]after target, menu[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]visual: give the target